// src/ast/ast.zen
// THE ast. The compiler, `@meta` and `gen_c` all consume these nodes.
//
// This file is the module's public surface and nothing else: a folder
// root is a file of starred re-exports, which is what makes a folder
// work. Everything a consumer needs is on this list, and a name absent
// from it is module-private on purpose.
//
// The shape, in four sentences, so nobody has to read four files to
// start:
//
//   - Every node is a struct carrying `span`, `leading` and
//     `trailing`, plus a `kind` enum whose variants carry the typed
//     node. `e.span` needs no match; `e.kind.match({..})` binds it.
//   - A child node is an id — `ExprId`, `TypeId`, `PatternId`,
//     `BlockId` — into `Ast`, which is the only thing that turns one
//     back into a node. Ids exist so a memoized query can key on a
//     node; they are indices, never addresses.
//   - Trivia lives in one list on `Ast` in source order, and a node
//     names a contiguous run of it.
//   - Declarations, members, arms, args, params, variants and
//     statements are held BY VALUE inside their parent. Only the four
//     id'd families close a cycle.
//
// `AST_CONTRACT.md`, beside this folder's parent, is the frozen
// description of what each node means and what invariants hold. Read
// that, not this implementation.

Pos*, Span*, TriviaKind*, Trivia*, TriviaRun*, no_trivia* = ast.ast_span
Ident*, QualifiedName* = ast.ast_span

ExprId*, TypeId*, PatternId*, BlockId* = ast.ast_id

BinOp*, UnOp*, Form*, LiteralKind*, Literal* = ast.ast_node
Type*, TypeKind*, Named*, Union*, FnType*, ArrayType* = ast.ast_node
Pattern*, PatternKind*, PatName*, Destructure* = ast.ast_node
Expr*, ExprKind*, Name*, Paren*, ArrayLit*, FixedArray* = ast.ast_node
Lambda*, Call*, Arg*, Match*, Arm*, Try*, Record* = ast.ast_node
Access*, Index*, Unary*, Binary*, Consume*, Meta* = ast.ast_node
Stmt*, StmtKind*, Bind*, ExprStmt*, Block* = ast.ast_node
Decl*, DeclKind*, Struct*, Enum*, Variant*, Alias* = ast.ast_node
Function*, Impl*, Import*, ImportName*, Const* = ast.ast_node
Member*, MemberKind*, Field*, Param*, TParam* = ast.ast_node
Module*, functions* = ast.ast_node

Ast* = ast.ast_arena

// A cursor position, and the node under it — the one query an editor
// needs that no other consumer does. PLAN.md stage 4.
NodeRef*, node_at*, expr_node_at*, in_span*, before*, inside* = ast.ast_find
